{"sections":[],"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every default placeholder ships two independent levers: a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"style"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (how big a footprint it expects to own) and, in SwiftUI, a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"theme"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (what color\/font it uses). On top of the default spinner, two alternative Loading placeholders cover the other common shapes a loading state takes: a pulsing skeleton, and a redacted mirror of the real content."}]},{"text":"`.compact` style","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"compact-style"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStatePlaceholderStyle","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" controls how much space a default placeholder expects to fill. Every default placeholder’s initializer takes a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"style:"},{"type":"text","text":" parameter, defaulting to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".standard"},{"type":"text","text":" — the full-screen treatment: a full-size icon, and, for the Loading spinner, filling all available space."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pass "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".compact"},{"type":"text","text":" to embed the same placeholder in a card or section instead of a whole screen: a smaller icon, smaller text, and — for the Loading spinner — no more forcing itself to fill the available space:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView(style: .compact)","ScreenStateDefaultLoadingUIView(style: .compact)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":".compact","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" always keeps a vertical icon-above-text layout, regardless of the device’s orientation — a card’s size is dictated by the card, not the device, unlike the automatic landscape-iPhone icon-beside-text switch ","type":"text"},{"code":".standard","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" makes on its own.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Alternative Loading placeholders","anchor":"Alternative-Loading-placeholders"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultLoadingView","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultLoadingUIView","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — the spinner — are what every default-wired "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateView"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateContainerView"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateViewController"},{"type":"text","text":" shows. Two opt-in alternatives cover the other common shapes a loading state takes:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateShimmerLoadingView","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateShimmerLoadingUIView","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": a pulsing skeleton of a circular avatar plus two text-line placeholders, for a generic “something’s coming” look that doesn’t need to know the real content’s shape."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateRedactedLoadingView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":": renders your real content view through SwiftUI’s "},{"code":".redacted(reason: .placeholder)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so the placeholder mirrors the exact shape of the content it’s standing in for. SwiftUI-only — "},{"code":"redacted(reason:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" has no UIKit equivalent."}]}]}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["ScreenStateShimmerLoadingView()","","ScreenStateRedactedLoadingView {","    ArticleRow(article: .placeholder)","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both respect Reduce Motion and Increase Contrast the same way the default spinner does; see "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Theming","anchor":"Theming"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStatesTheme","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" lets a SwiftUI app theme every default placeholder at once — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tint"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"titleFont"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"messageFont"},{"type":"text","text":" — instead of passing a fully custom placeholder view at every call site. Set it once via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View.screenStatesTheme(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" on a container view, and every default placeholder beneath it in the view hierarchy (including "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateShimmerLoadingView","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") picks it up:"}]},{"code":["MyScreenView()","    .screenStatesTheme(ScreenStatesTheme(tint: .indigo, titleFont: .title2, messageFont: .callout))"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Any property left "},{"typ